│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ vectorize_balanced_packing_hot_loop                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The dominant cost of the algorithm is `balanced_packing`, which runs an O(num_layers ×    │
│                          │ num_groups) Python loop where each iteration does `min(...)` over generator packs AND     │
│                          │ indexes into a torch tensor (`indices` iterates over 0-d tensors — each access is a slow  │
│                          │ tensor-to-Python conversion). Converting the sorted indices and weights to plain Python   │
│                          │ lists once per call removes all tensor overhead from the hot loop. Additionally, we only  │
│                          │ need `min` over packs that aren't full — tracking the pack candidates in a small list and │
│                          │ using `min(candidates, key=...)` on a plain list is dramatically faster than a generator  │
│                          │ over all packs with a conditional. Since `num_groups` is at most a few hundred,           │
│                          │ pure-Python lists are far faster than tensor ops per element. This cuts algorithm         │
│                          │ execution time substantially (improving `times_algorithm` and the speed score) while      │
│                          │ producing identical packing results, so balancedness is preserved. We also vectorize      │
│                          │ `replicate_experts`'s per-iteration division (weight/logcnt each iteration recomputes a   │
│                          │ full tensor division on all experts; we can update only the changed entry) — actually     │
│                          │ simpler: keep it but compute on the smaller per-node slice which it already is; the main  │
│                          │ win is balanced_packing.                                                                  │
