│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The main runtime bottleneck is `balanced_packing`: it runs a pure-Python double loop over │
│                          │ `num_layers x num_groups` items (called once for groups→nodes and once for physical       │
│                          │ experts→GPUs), each iteration doing Python-level list operations and `min()`. This        │
│                          │ dominates the algorithm time (speed_score is currently 0.00).                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ We can vectorize across layers: keep `pack_weights` and `pack_items` as tensors of shape  │
│                          │ , and only loop over the `num_groups` placement steps. In each step we place the          │
│                          │ next-heaviest remaining item of every layer simultaneously: mask out full packs with      │
│                          │ +inf, take an `argmin` over packs (which preserves the original min-index tie-breaking),  │
│                          │ and update state with advanced indexing. This reduces the Python loop count from          │
│                          │ `num_layers * num_groups` to `num_groups`, with each iteration doing a handful of         │
│                          │ vectorized tensor ops, and keeps identical greedy semantics (sort descending, place each  │
│                          │ item in the lightest non-full pack).                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The greedy packing logic and outputs are unchanged, so GPU/ node balancedness is          │
│                          │ preserved, while algorithm runtime drops substantially, improving the speed score and     │
│                          │ thus the combined score.                                                                  │
