│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ vectorized_numpy_eplb_pipeline                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Restructure the EPLB algorithm as a NumPy-based pipeline, replacing the slow per-layer,   │
│                          │ per-item Python loops (the O(layers × experts × packs) scans in `balanced_packing` and    │
│                          │ the repeated full-tensor reductions in `replicate_experts`) with operations vectorized    │
│                          │ across all layers simultaneously.                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key structural changes:                                                                   │
│                          │ 1. **Batched greedy packing**: instead of looping layer-by-layer and item-by-item with a  │
│                          │ `min()` scan over packs, `balanced_packing` now processes all layers in lockstep — one    │
│                          │ vectorized `argmin` over a `` load matrix per sorted item — preserving the exact          │
│                          │ LPT-with-cardinality greedy semantics (including tie-breaking by lowest pack index) at a  │
│                          │ fraction of the cost.                                                                     │
│                          │ 2. **Incremental replication**: `replicate_experts` maintains a running `weight/count`    │
│                          │ ratio matrix, updating only the selected expert's ratio each iteration instead of         │
│                          │ recomputing the full division and max over all experts.                                   │
│                          │ 3. **Unified NumPy dataflow**: all intermediate permutation/gather/scatter steps of the   │
│                          │ hierarchical policy run on NumPy arrays (via `np.take_along_axis` and row-wise scatter    │
│                          │ inverse permutations), avoiding per-op PyTorch dispatch overhead; results convert back to │
│                          │ torch int64 tensors only at the entry-point boundary.                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The outputs (physical_to_logical_map, logical_to_physical_map, expert_count) are          │
│                          │ identical in shape, dtype, and semantics to the original, but the algorithm runtime drops │
│                          │ from quadratic-in-items Python loops to compact vectorized passes, improving the speed    │
│                          │ score while keeping the same greedy balancing quality.                                    │
