│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ vectorize_balanced_packing_greedy                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The main performance bottleneck is `balanced_packing`: it runs a pure-Python double loop  │
│                          │ (num_layers × num_groups iterations with scalar `min(...)` calls), and it's invoked twice │
│                          │ per rebalance. The combined score is dragged down by a speed_score of 0.00                │
│                          │ (times_algorithm 0.58).                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The fix vectorizes the inner loop across layers while keeping the *exact same* greedy     │
│                          │ LPT-with-capacity policy (each item goes to the least-loaded pack that still has          │
│                          │ capacity, ties broken by lowest pack index, same as the original `min(...,                │
│                          │ key=pack_weights.__getitem__)`). Now there are only `num_groups` Python iterations, each  │
│                          │ performing batched tensor ops over all layers at once, instead of `num_layers *           │
│                          │ num_groups` scalar iterations. This preserves the balancedness quality of the original    │
│                          │ algorithm (no approximation like snake/zigzag packing) while reducing the Python-level    │
│                          │ work by roughly a factor of `num_layers`, directly improving the execution-time component │
│                          │ of the combined score.                                                                    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
