│ patch_name               │ gpu_swap_refinement_pass                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Add a greedy local-search refinement pass after Step 3 of the hierarchical algorithm.     │
│                          │ After `balanced_packing` assigns physical experts to GPUs, per-GPU loads may still be     │
│                          │ unbalanced (GPU balancedness is only 0.66). Since each GPU holds a fixed number of        │
│                          │ physical experts, we can swap experts between the most-loaded and least-loaded GPU within │
│                          │ each node (keeping pack sizes constant), choosing the pair whose weight difference best   │
│                          │ halves the load gap. This is fully vectorized across all (layer, node) rows, iterated at  │
│                          │ most 20 times, and stops early when no swap reduces the global max load. It reuses the    │
│                          │ existing `pack_index`/`rank_in_pack` plumbing so the downstream `phy2pphy` construction   │
│                          │ is unchanged. This should substantially improve GPU balancedness at negligible runtime    │
│                          │ cost (a few vectorized ops per iteration, versus the expensive Python loops in            │
│                          │ `balanced_packing`).                                                                      │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
