│ patch_description        │ The current snake-deal packing matches greedy quality (GPU 0.66 / expert 0.25) at zero    │
│                          │ algorithm time. To push balancedness higher, I add a fully vectorized local-search        │
│                          │ refinement pass after the snake packing: compute pack loads with a single `scatter_add`,  │
│                          │ then repeatedly find the heaviest-loaded and lightest-loaded pack per row, and swap the   │
│                          │ heaviest item of the overloaded pack with the lightest item of the underloaded pack       │
│                          │ whenever it provably shrinks the max-min load gap. Each refinement round is a handful of  │
│                          │ vectorized tensor ops over all layers simultaneously, with an early exit when no row      │
│                          │ improves, so the runtime overhead stays tiny while the packing quality strictly improves  │
│                          │ over plain greedy/snake (which never swaps). This refinement is applied in both packing   │
│                          │ steps (groups→nodes and physical experts→GPUs), so both GPU-level and expert-level        │
│                          │ balancedness improve while keeping the exact output format.                               │
