                        Patch Metadata - Gen 17/100 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/3                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ lpt_replication_and_vectorized_packing                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ The expert balancedness (0.25) is the weakest metric. The current `replicate_experts`     │
│                          │ greedily replicates the expert with the highest weight/count ratio, which is a myopic     │
│                          │ heuristic and under-uses redundancy. Instead, we do a proper LPT over post-replication    │
│                          │ loads: treat each logical expert's weight as being divided among its replicas; when we    │
│                          │ must add a replica, we pick the expert whose removal best reduces the maximum per-expert  │
│                          │ replica load. Concretely, sorting experts by weight descending and assigning each replica │
│                          │ (in that order, including the first `num_log` mandatory replicas) to keep replica loads   │
│                          │ balanced yields a much better LPT-style solution: each logical expert of weight w gets    │
│                          │ either ceil/floor of total/num_log replicas such that w/c is as uniform as possible. This │
│                          │ directly targets the expert balancedness metric (which measures how uniform the           │
│                          │ per-replica loads w_i/c_i are).                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Additionally, `balanced_packing` is currently a slow Python double loop (times_algorithm  │
│                          │ 0.49). Replace it with the vectorized masked-argmin LPT loop validated in a prior program │
│                          │ (which achieved times_algorithm 0.01), processing all rows in lockstep.                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new replication strategy: sort experts descending by weight; compute a target replica │
│                          │ load T = total_weight / num_phy; for each expert in descending order, assign c_i = max(1, │
│                          │ round(w_i / T)) replicas, then fix up the total to exactly num_phy greedily by adjusting  │
│                          │ the counts that most reduce the max deviation. This is a one-shot assignment with a small │
│                          │ greedy fix-up, much faster than the per-replica loop and better balanced.                 │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0196                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
