│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ flat_lpt_replication_and_gpu_packing                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the three-level hierarchical pipeline (group→node packing, node-local             │
│                          │ replication, node-local GPU packing) with a flat, direct two-stage scheme: (1) decide     │
│                          │ replica counts per logical expert with a greedy loop that always replicates the expert    │
│                          │ with the highest per-replica load (weight/logcnt), and (2) build a flat list of all       │
│                          │ physical replicas (each with load weight/logcnt), sort them descending, and run one       │
│                          │ batched LPT `balanced_packing` across *all* GPUs. This removes the intermediate node      │
│                          │ constraint that forced heavy experts to stay within a node's expert budget, so the greedy │
│                          │ LPT sees the whole GPU pool and both the expert-level loads (weight/logcnt) and the       │
│                          │ GPU-level loads are directly minimized by the same LPT that already scored well (0.66 gpu │
│                          │ balancedness). Post-replication loads feeding LPT (instead of the naive load/count ratio  │
│                          │ heuristic deciding placement) directly target the weakest metric, expert balancedness.    │
│                          │ The algorithm is also simpler: one replication loop + one LPT pass instead of two LPT     │
│                          │ passes plus gather/scatter plumbing, so execution time stays small.                       │
