│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ lpt_swap_refine_packing                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The current algorithm already vectorizes the LPT greedy across layers, but its packing    │
│                          │ quality (especially expert-level balancedness, 0.25) is limited by plain                  │
│                          │ cardinality-constrained LPT, which is only a 4/3-approximation and leaves local           │
│                          │ imbalance. My key insight: after the greedy assignment, most residual imbalance is        │
│                          │ pairwise — the heaviest pack contains small items that could trade places with large      │
│                          │ items in the lightest pack. I add a vectorized-across-packs, per-layer local-search       │
│                          │ refinement that repeatedly swaps the smallest-weight item in the most-loaded pack with    │
│                          │ the largest-weight item in the least-loaded pack whenever the swap strictly reduces the   │
│                          │ spread. Swapping preserves both the cardinality constraint and rank-in-pack uniqueness    │
│                          │ (the two items simply exchange packs and inherit each other's slots). Since               │
│                          │ `balanced_packing` is used both for node packing (Step 1) and GPU packing (Step 3), the   │
│                          │ refinement improves balance at every level of the hierarchy while adding only a few cheap │
│                          │ CPU tensor ops per round. The replication step is unchanged (its greedy weight/logcnt     │
│                          │ split is already near-optimal for a divisible-load model), keeping execution time near    │
│                          │ the current 0.01s while improving both GPU and expert balancedness scores.                │
