│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ lpt_swap_refinement_balancer                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Structural redesign around a reusable "pack-and-refine" kernel architecture:              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Modular packing pipeline**: The packing logic is decomposed into three small,        │
│                          │ composable primitives — `_lpt_packing` (vectorized batched LPT seed), `_refine_packing`   │
│                          │ (vectorized local-search swap refinement), and `_rank_from_pack_index` (rank recovery     │
│                          │ from an arbitrary pack assignment). `balanced_packing` is now an orchestrator of these    │
│                          │ stages instead of a monolithic loop.                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Local-search refinement stage (new)**: After the greedy LPT seed, a fully vectorized │
│                          │ refinement repeatedly swaps items between the currently heaviest and lightest pack of     │
│                          │ each row. Each round evaluates two swap candidates (heaviest item in max-pack ↔ lightest  │
│                          │ item in min-pack, and lightest item in max-pack ↔ heaviest item in min-pack) and applies  │
│                          │ whichever best reduces the max-min spread. Swaps only occur when they strictly reduce the │
│                          │ spread, so refinement monotonically improves balance. This directly targets the GPU       │
│                          │ balancedness metric, since both step 1 (groups → nodes) and step 3 (physical experts →    │
│                          │ GPUs) use this kernel.                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Rank decoupling**: Ranks within a pack are no longer coupled to insertion order;     │
│                          │ they are derived from the final pack assignment via a stable sort. This makes any pack    │
│                          │ permutation (e.g., produced by refinement) a valid first-class result, since within-pack  │
│                          │ ordering is semantically arbitrary downstream.                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Faster, fully tensorized seed**: The LPT loop operates entirely on stacked tensors   │
│                          │ with no per-row Python iteration or host-device sync inside the loop, and explicit guards │
│                          │ for degenerate cases (`num_packs == 1`, capacity 1) avoid wasted work.                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The hierarchical three-stage data flow (groups → nodes, replication within node, physical │
│                          │ → GPUs) and the public `rebalance_experts` contract (inputs, outputs, shapes, semantics)  │
│                          │ are unchanged.                                                                            │
